      "claim": "FIXED",
      "final_text": "I fixed two problems in `sim/src/mcsim/physics.py`, and the sprint-jump scenario I tried now matches the oracle for all 40 ticks. The 25 visible regression scenarios and the unit tests also pass. I didn't write any new scenarios beyond that one, so the wall fixture and strafe or backward sprint-jumps are covered only by the visible regressions.\n\n- **Sprint-jump boost:** `jump_from_ground` only applied the +0.2 horizontal boost when the player was not on the ground. That was backwards, because a jump always starts from the ground, so the boost never fired. I removed the `not p.on_ground` condition.\n- **Air acceleration:** while airborne, `travel` reused the ground acceleration formula. In the real game it is a flat 0.02, or 0.026 when sprinting. This was the cause of the divergence from tick 6.\n\nSTATUS: FIXED",
